(text "XTAL - 8 MHz  |  ECS ECX-33Q  |  ECS-80-8-33Q-JES-TR  |  Pierce oscillator" (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 14.00 0) (effects (font (size 2.2 2.2) (bold yes)) (justify left top)) (uuid "b489b6c2-420f-483b-922e-52feada6f874"))
(text "House-common passives: load caps 12 pF C0G 0603, Rext 0R jumper, Rf 1M (DNP). Typical use: STM32 HSE, CAN, AVR." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 19.30 0) (effects (font (size 1.27 1.27)) (justify left top)) (uuid "55f5ae98-33a2-41fe-8d54-d3e1dfbf2277"))
(text "DESIGN EQUATIONS - 8 MHz crystal, ECS-80-8-33Q-JES-TR (ECS ECX-33Q); refs: ST AN2867 / TI SZZA043 / TI SLAA322\nCrystal: CL = 8 pF, ESR max = 500 ohm\n  C0 max = 7 pF, drive level max = 100 uW (datasheet), fundamental mode. Uses: STM32 HSE, CAN, AVR\nLoad caps: C1 = C2 = 2*(CL - Cs), Cs = 2.0 pF (pin + trace, edit for your layout) = 12.0 pF -> 12 pF C0G 5% (house value)\n  Effective CL = C1*C2/(C1+C2) + Cs = 6 + 2.0 = 8.0 pF (+0.0 pF vs spec)\nPulling: S = C1m/(2*(C0+CL)^2) ~ 6.7 ppm/pF (C1m ~3 fF typ, assumed) ; 5% cap tol -> dCL +/-0.30 pF -> +/-2.0 ppm\nOscillation margin: gm_crit = 4*ESR*(2*pi*f)^2*(C0+CL)^2 = 1.137 mA/V\n  Gain margin = gm(osc)/gm_crit >= 5 -> oscillator gm must exceed 5.68 mA/V (check MCU datasheet HSE/LSE gm)\nDrive level @ 1.0 Vpp on XOUT: DL = ESR*(2*pi*f*(C0+CL)*Vpp/(2*sqrt2))^2 = 35.53 uW vs 100 uW max -> OK\nDrive level @ 3.3 Vpp on XOUT: DL = ESR*(2*pi*f*(C0+CL)*Vpp/(2*sqrt2))^2 = 386.93 uW vs 100 uW max -> EXCEEDED - fit Rext\nRext (series, XOUT side): start value 1/(2*pi*f*C2) = 1.66 kohm ; fitted 0R (house jumper) - populate only if DL exceeded,\n  then re-check gain margin with ESR -> ESR + Rext. Rf 1M (house) shown DNP: fit only if the oscillator has no internal feedback resistor.\nLayout: C1/C2 and crystal within ~5 mm of the pins, GND guard ring, no signals under the crystal, return C1/C2 to the oscillator GND pin." (exclude_from_sim no) (at 20.32 128.00 0) (effects (font (size 1.45 1.45)) (justify left top)) (uuid "5e954285-6978-4807-9c10-844535680444"))
